<div class="page">
  <div class="header-logo">
    <div class="logo-text">The Guild</div>
    <div class="university-name">Houston Baptist University</div>
  </div>
  <h2 class="section-title">2014 SPRING NEWSLETTER</h2>

  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="column">
      <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold;">Greetings from the President</h3>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>Some years ago HBU had a campaign, "Write Your Own Story!" It was a brilliant marketing campaign which proved to be successful for the university. It was a wonderful opportunity for alumni did indeed write their stories of their lives. The campaign emphasized the benefits of an experience and showed a unique university family that was still and today, inviting in a way that stands out among universities.</p>
        <p>The reporting of <span data-field="reporting_topic">{{ reporting_topic }}</span> for a 12-year vision for HBU which was led by President <span data-field="president_name">{{ president_name }}</span>. Soon and created from ideas and initiatives from faculty, staff, students, trustees and alumni. The institution states: "The vision we have for our university begins with a story. It is about <span data-field="vision_summary">{{ vision_summary }}</span>."</p>
        <p>Ladies, we are a part of this wonderful story of HBU as we help Dr. <span data-field="dr_name">{{ dr_name }}</span> promote the growth and development of this blessed university. The Lord desires that we discover His plan, and we are all called to be part of His plan. We are all part of His plan. We are all part of His plan.</p>
        <p>We all know and have experienced the truth that God's word is timeless and is a treasure to us. We also know that the Lord is faithful and that He is good. We also know that the Lord is faithful and that He is good. In John 6:14-15, Jesus asked, "Where are we to buy bread, so that these may eat?" Christ knew all who were following Him, because He was doing miracles. He knew that they were coming to Him to eat of the bread. But they did not understand that He was coming to give them the bread of life, but only the physical bread. He was only a man, but He was the Son of God. He was the bread of life. He was the bread of life.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column">
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>wants us to serve. We ultimately serve Jesus, and when we step out in faith and obedience to Him, He does great things in us and through us. If you think your "yes" to serving has little or no influence, please think again and remember this: we cannot serve a God who is not worthy of our service. We cannot serve a God who is not worthy of our service. We cannot serve a God who is not worthy of our service.</p>
        <p>This is my last newsletter to you as your President. It has been an honor and a privilege to serve you in this capacity. Your prayers, notes, letters, cards, phone calls, emails and texts have all been a great source of strength and encouragement for me for the past <span data-field="time_period">{{ time_period }}</span>. I am so grateful for your support.</p>
        <p>As Sharon Saunders often quotes, "We all stand on the shoulders of those who came before us." Thank you to all the Past Presidents who paved the way for me to serve as President. We are all part of a legacy of faith and service to our university.</p>
        <p>As <span data-field="president_name">{{ president_name }}</span>, I look forward to serving under the leadership of Jan Witham and the new Guild Board. I am excited about the future of HBU and the Guild. I am excited about the future of HBU and the Guild.</p>
        <p>Through HBU's "Write Your Own Story" campaign ended years ago, I encourage each of you to take this opportunity to "write your own story" of how HBU has touched, shaped, or changed your life. I invite you to join the Guild. I stand with you in this endeavor.</p>
        <p>In His Love and Service,</p>
        <div class="signature-block">
          <div class="signature-line"></div>
          <p style="font-weight: bold;">Debra Perich</p>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size: 10px; margin-top: 30px;">*Trust in the Lord with all your heart, and do not rely on your own insight. In all your ways acknowledge Him, and He will make straight your paths.* - Proverbs 3:5-6</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h2 class="section-title" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 10px;">Silver Tea</h2>
  <div class="content-block" style="display: flex; gap: 30px; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div style="flex: 1;">
      <p>Wednesday, <span data-field="date">{{ date }}</span> what a glorious day for The Guild Silver Tea, and a fun day as well! The house was fabulous, the food was delicious, the music was perfect, and ... and the Lord answered our prayers giving us great weather as we gathered together to honor Judy Graham for her Christian leadership and commitment to HBU and The Guild. Those attending celebrated a wonderful atmosphere of Christian fellowship.</p>
      <p>Jana and Scott Arnoldy opened their beautiful home to The Guild with kindness and hospitality to raise scholarship dollars for HBU's School of Education and School of Christian Thought. In addition, Jana Arnoldy created floral arrangements and placed them throughout the house and grounds to be enjoyed by all.</p>
      <p>Co-chairs, Donna Goeser and Cheryl Kaminski, along with their committees, planned it down to the wire and executed it with grace and excellence. The event was a huge success, which is the first introduction it was! The beautiful guitar music by <span data-field="musician_name">{{ musician_name }}</span>, the delicious food, the wonderful fellowship by Latin guitarist, Guillermo Serpas, could be enjoyed by everyone whether mingling inside the house or outside on the grounds. It was a perfect day for a Silver Tea!</p>
      <p>We are extremely blessed with a wonderful President and First Lady, Robert and Sue Sloan, to work with and support in this great endeavor for HBU. We are also very thankful to the underwriters and donors who have made this year's Silver Tea and our Guild Scholarship Program a success!</p>
      <p style="text-align: center; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 30px;">"To God Give The Glory Great Things He Hath Done!"</p>
    </div>
    <div style="flex: 1; text-align: center;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_1.jpg" alt="Honorary Guest" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
      <p style="font-size: 12px; margin-top: 5px;">Honorary Guest Judy Graham and husband Gerald Graham</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

