<div class="page">
  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="column" style="flex: 1;">
      <h3 style="font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold;">The Guild Institute in Christian Family Studies</h3>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 30px; margin-top: 20px;">
        <div style="flex: 1;">
          <img src="placeholder_image_7.jpg" alt="Lee Strobel speaking at Convocation" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
          <p style="font-size: 12px; margin-top: 5px;">Lee Strobel speaking at Convocation.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="flex: 1;">
          <img src="placeholder_image_8.jpg" alt="Sharon Saunders, Debra Perich, Lee Strobel, Anne Roper, Jane Caldwell" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
          <p style="font-size: 12px; margin-top: 5px;">Sharon Saunders, Debra Perich, Lee Strobel, Anne Roper, Jane Caldwell</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="content-block" style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <p>The Guild Institute in Christian Family Studies welcomed Lee Strobel at HBU Convocation on February 19, 2014. Lee Strobel is a recent addition to the faculty and is a renowned investigative journalist, author, and speaker. He has written over 800 books including The Case for Christ and The Case for Reason. His presentation at the Convocation was a powerful testimony to the students in their "unexpected adventure" as they walk through the challenges of life and faith. He spoke about the eternal nature of life and light of the world.</p>
        <p>Following Convocation, a luncheon honoring the Guild's leadership was held. The event was a wonderful opportunity for the Guild to thank its leaders and to share in fellowship. The Committee Chairs for this event were Anne Roper and Jane Caldwell.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column" style="text-align: right;">
      <img src="placeholder_image_9.jpg" alt="Faculty members attending luncheon" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;">
      <p style="font-size: 12px; margin-top: 5px;">Faculty members attending luncheon.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="two-column">
    <div class="column" style="flex: 1;">
      <div class="header-logo">
        <div class="logo-text">The Guild</div>
        <div class="university-name">Houston Baptist University</div>
      </div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>Letter from the Editor</p>
        <p>As we reach the end of another Guild year and prepare for the more leisurely summer ahead, it's time to reflect on the accomplishments of this past year. HBU has been a beehive of activity throughout the year. Officers and Committee Chairs of The Guild have never been busier.</p>
        <p>As Newsletter Editor for two years, I have had the opportunity to work with this amazing group of women. On behalf of all of us, I want to thank them for their service. I especially want to thank Debra Perich, our President, for all she has accomplished for HBU and for The Guild during her two-year term. She has been a tireless advocate for HBU and has given much of her time to Guild activities. In large part, it is because of her leadership that we have continued success in awarding scholarships in graduate education to qualified students.</p>
        <p>Let's enjoy our summer vacation and return in the fall ready to support our new President, Jan Witham.</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 50px; text-align: right;">— Georgia Byrnes</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="column" style="text-align: center;">
      <img src="placeholder_logo_large.png" alt="Large Guild Logo" style="max-width: 250px;">
    </div>
  </div>
</div>